@startuml h2-sequence-VERIFIED_AS_DEPLOYED
' =============================================================================
' STATUS: VERIFIED_AS_DEPLOYED
' Same provenance as the companion class diagram
' (h2-class-VERIFIED_AS_DEPLOYED.puml) -- confirmed on the live host, not
' assumed. No architectural delta from REVIEWED_CANDIDATE_PRE_DEPLOYMENT.
'
' Flow 1 (normal enriched delivery) is deployed and code-verified via a
' controlled fixture on the real host, but full live confirmation is
' currently blocked on a credential-provisioning gap, not a code or
' deployment defect: the intel webhook and all three provider API-key SSM
' parameters do not yet exist (confirmed via ssm:DescribeParameters).
'
' Flow 2 (provider failure/degraded) is the flow actually exercised live at
' H2_T0: with every provider credential absent, ThreatIntelBroker.enrich_ip
' returned {status: missing_credential} for greynoise/virustotal/shodan
' (fail-open, no exception), build_session_summary_payload still produced a
' valid, deliverable embed, and CredentialCache.get() for the intel webhook
' itself also correctly returned None -- delivery skipped with a logged
' warning (credential_unavailable), never a crash. This is the same
' fail-open contract test_h2_enrichment_pipeline.py already proved offline,
' now independently reproduced on the deployed bytes.
'
' Flow 3 (immediate legacy alert, no broker edge) is independently confirmed
' live: the real process's own ops log shows delivery_success entries for
' the legacy channel both before and after H2_T0 (credential_available for
' /patriotpot/2026-control/discord-webhook), continuing uninterrupted
' through the H2 restart -- exactly the architectural independence this
' flow exists to show.
' =============================================================================

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' UPSTREAM DEPENDENCY NOTICE (added 2026-09-23, after P0 recovery)
'
' This diagram depicts what happens to Cowrie telemetry ONCE IT EXISTS. It
' does not depict whether it exists. That is the Cowrie session lifecycle,
' documented separately in:
'     docs/diagrams/cowrie-session-lifecycle-P0-FAULT-POINTS.puml
'
' RESEARCH-INTEGRITY NOTE: when H2 was validated and closed on 2026-09-20,
' three upstream defects (evidence/2026-09-23-p0-recovery/) were silently
' preventing Cowrie from emitting cowrie.command.input at all -- 16,070
' successful logins produced zero commands. H2's own validation used
' synthetic fixtures replayed directly through the deployed code path, so
' those results remain valid for the pipeline itself. But H2's REAL-WORLD
' input was empty during that window. Any analysis of live enrichment
' output before 2026-09-23 must account for that, and no conclusion about
' attacker behaviour may be drawn from the absence of enriched session
' summaries in that period.
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

title H2 Sequence Diagrams -- VERIFIED_AS_DEPLOYED

== Flow 1: Normal enriched session-summary delivery ==

participant "Cowrie JSON log" as Log
participant "discord-monitor.py\n(queue_line / flush_expired_clusters)" as Main
participant "SessionClusterManager" as ClusterMgr
participant "SessionCluster" as Cluster
participant "ThreatIntelWorker" as Worker
participant "ThreatIntelBroker" as Broker
participant "EnrichmentCache" as Cache
participant "GreyNoise / VirusTotal / Shodan" as Providers
participant "build_session_summary_payload()" as Builder
participant "Discord webhook\n(intel channel)" as Webhook

Log -> Main : raw_line (cowrie.login.success)
Main -> ClusterMgr : observe(event, now)
ClusterMgr -> Cluster : record_event(event)
Main -> ClusterMgr : flush_expired(now)
ClusterMgr --> Main : [cluster] (window elapsed)
Main -> Worker : try_submit(cluster)
Worker --> Main : True (non-blocking, accepted)
note right of Main
  Ingestion (offset consumption) is never
  blocked: try_submit() returns immediately
  regardless of provider latency.
end note

group background thread
  Worker -> Broker : enrich_ip(cluster.src_ip)
  Broker -> Cache : get(cache_key)
  Cache --> Broker : None (miss)
  Broker -> Providers : lookup_ip(ip, api_key, timeout)  [x3, parallel]
  Providers --> Broker : ProviderResponse(status=ok, normalized={...})
  Broker -> Cache : set(cache_key, envelope, ttl)
  Broker --> Worker : {greynoise: {...}, virustotal: {...}, shodan: {...}}
end

Main -> Worker : drain_completed()
Worker --> Main : [(cluster, enrichment)]
Main -> Builder : build_session_summary_payload(cluster, enrichment)
Builder --> Main : Discord embed payload\n(base Cowrie fields + enrichment fields)
Main -> Main : enqueue_pending(state, flush_id, payload, "intel")
Main -> Webhook : POST payload (pending_intel drain)
Webhook --> Main : 2xx

== Flow 2: Provider failure / degraded -- summary still delivers ==

Log -> Main : raw_line
Main -> ClusterMgr : observe(event, now)
Main -> ClusterMgr : flush_expired(now)
ClusterMgr --> Main : [cluster]
Main -> Worker : try_submit(cluster)

group background thread
  Worker -> Broker : enrich_ip(cluster.src_ip)
  Broker -> Providers : lookup_ip(...)  [x3]
  Providers --> Broker : timeout / 429 / 5xx / raised exception
  note right of Broker
    Fail-open by construction: any exception,
    timeout, rate-limit, or server error
    becomes a status envelope for that
    provider alone. enrich_ip() never raises.
  end note
  Broker --> Worker : {greynoise: {status: "unavailable"/"timeout"/\n  "rate_limited"/"error"}, ...}
end

Main -> Worker : drain_completed()
Worker --> Main : [(cluster, enrichment)]  ' enrichment may even be None\n  ' if the broker call itself raised
Main -> Builder : build_session_summary_payload(cluster, enrichment)
Builder --> Main : Discord embed payload\n(enrichment fields show the failure\n status string, base fields intact)
Main -> Main : enqueue_pending(state, flush_id, payload, "intel")
Main -> Webhook : POST payload (pending_intel drain)
Webhook --> Main : 2xx

note over Main, Webhook
  CRITICAL INVARIANT: this POST happens regardless of which/how many
  providers failed. worker=None, backlog-exhausted (try_submit -> False),
  and an all-providers-exception flush all reach the same enqueue_pending
  call -- see BaseAlertSurvivesEnrichmentFailureTests.
end note

== Flow 3: Immediate legacy alert -- ThreatIntelBroker never instantiated ==

Log -> Main : raw_line (priority event,\ne.g. cowrie.login.success)
Main -> ClusterMgr : observe(event, now)
Main -> Main : format_alert(event)
note right of Main
  format_alert() reads ONLY the raw Cowrie
  event dict. No SessionClusterManager
  enrichment field, no ThreatIntelBroker
  reference, no EnrichmentCache reference --
  this call has no edge to any box in the
  "threat_intel" package of the class
  diagram at all.
end note
Main -> Main : enqueue_pending(state, item_id,\n  payload, "legacy")
participant "Discord webhook\n(legacy channel)" as LegacyWebhook
Main -> LegacyWebhook : POST payload (pending_legacy drain)
LegacyWebhook --> Main : 2xx

note over Main
  This delivery path is architecturally
  independent of enrichment success, failure,
  latency, or even whether a
  ThreatIntelBroker/Worker was ever
  constructed for this process. It is not
  merely decoupled in practice -- there is no
  code path from queue_line()'s immediate-
  alert branch that can reach the broker.
end note

@enduml
